The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (cdclk > 312000)
```
Reason:
This condition does not account for the new cdclk values (324/326.4), leading to incorrect voltage level assignments for cdclk inputs greater than 312000 but less than or equal to 326400.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (cdclk > 326400)
	return 3;
else if (cdclk > 312000)
	return 2;
```
Reason:
These updated conditions correctly incorporate the new cdclk thresholds, ensuring that voltage levels are assigned accurately for the new 324/326.4 cdclk values, thus improving system performance and stability.

